# Twin of celpole_z_above_tol with CRVAL2 = -30.000000001: celset's
# z = cos(latp) cos(lat0) = 1.6e-11 is WITHIN its 1e-10 tolerance, so wcslib
# takes the "celestial north pole at the native pole" branch (lngp = lng0 +
# phip - phi0 - 180) although z != 0. A tolerance tighter than 1.6e-11 (or
# an exact z == 0 test) takes the ill-conditioned atan2 branch instead.
# Synthetic.
NOTE pipeline: celset z = 1.6e-11, within the 1e-10 tolerance (nonzero)
GRID 1 512 9 1 512 9
SKYGRID 0 350 8 -80 80 5
HEADER
NAXIS   = 2
NAXIS1  = 512
NAXIS2  = 512
CTYPE1  = 'RA---CAR'
CTYPE2  = 'DEC--CAR'
CRVAL1  = 10.0
CRVAL2  = -30.000000001
CRPIX1  = 256.5
CRPIX2  = 256.5
CDELT1  = -0.1
CDELT2  = 0.1
PV1_2   = -30.0
LONPOLE = 150.0
LATPOLE = 90.0
